solutions.latex:
\exfigure{1628_q25_s1}

For $f(x)$ to be a probability density function, the total area under it must be 1. The region is a triangle with base $h$ and height 1:
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{1}{2}\times 1\times h &= 1\\ h &= 2\end{aligned}$$

\exfigure{1357_q24_s1}

The parabola section meets the horizontal section $F(x) = 1$ at $x = 1.8$:
$$F(1.8) = \dfrac{25}{116}\left(1.8^2 + 5.4 - 4\right) = 1$$

